# Story 37: Rysh Mode (## commands) (40s)
# Hook: Hash-hash is rysh mode -- the control panel for your whole workspace.
# Duration: 40s
# Source: story-037-rysh-mode.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 6

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Hash-hash is rysh mode -- the control panel for your whole workspace.

[00:03.0 --> 00:09.0]
Start rysh, then double-Escape until the prompt shows hash-hash. System commands inject their output right into the active pane.

[00:09.0 --> 00:18.0]
Help lists every system command -- panes, tabs, lanes, sharing, agents, and more.

[00:18.0 --> 00:28.0]
Try one: pane info reports the active pane's details, all without leaving the keyboard.

[00:28.0 --> 00:38.0]
One caution: a line starting with hash-hash-greater-than is not a command. Those are pipeline events, forwarded straight to NATS instead of being run.

[00:38.0 --> 00:40.0]
Rysh mode is how you drive the multiplexer itself.

